finding('TA101-01','shared_semantic_error',['Taanit 9a:10','Taanit 9a:11'],['ta101.claims.0067','ta101.positions.0057','ta101.edges.0042'],['ta.resume016.abahu.rereading','ta.resume016.abahu.rereading.p','ta.resume016.abahu.rereading.u'], 'Both first readings translate the rereading as they feared. The immediate argument is removal of protective clouds and the congregation becoming visible/exposed. Added local Rashi explicitly explains נתראו and ואתחזיאו. Agreement is a shared error, not independent confirmation. The unpointed original spelling remains preserved.','Revise translation to became visible/exposed with source/commentary distinction; retain original records and recheck dependent support to cloud departure.','high')
finding('TA101-02','producer_attribution_omission',['Taanit 9a:7'],['ta101.attributions.0078','ta101.utterances.0073'],['ta.resume016.mother.warning.a','ta.resume016.mother.warning.u','ta.resume016.mother.warning.p'],'אמרה ליה explicitly introduces the mother speaking. Producer prose identifies her but structured attribution/utterance voice remains anonymous and holder empty. This is layer loss, not missing narrative content.','Preserve mother as character speaker, and warning rather than narrator-certified causal claim.')
