finding('TA101-04','producer_attribution_omission',['Taanit 9a:5'],['ta101.attributions.0071'],['ta.resume016.folly.verse.a','ta.resume016.folly.verse.u'],'Quoted-authority typing correctly recognizes Proverbs, but no structured speaker preserves the explicitly reciting child (דיתיב ואמר). Narrative prose contains it; attribution layer does not.','Retain quoted authority and add reciter/speaker distinction; do not count the proverb as an independently authored child doctrine.')
finding('TA101-05','producer_relation_omission',['Taanit 7b:15'],['ta101.edges.0019','ta101.claims.0024'],['ta.resume011.deeds.before','ta.resume011.mercy.strengthen','ta.resume011.mercy.answer'],'כל שכן records preference for deeds rectified beforehand. Producer retains the claim but its graph has only the remedy answer, omitting this explicit relation. This is an edge omission, not a missing claim.','Add a faithful qualification/a-fortiori relation or document a schema-appropriate equivalent, with exact endpoints and source span.')
